enchilada: SLPI (sensor DSP): read-only probe (slpi=1), sensors round 1

The OnePlus 6's IMU (BMI160, SPI), light/proximity (TMD3725, I2C 0x39) and magnetometer sit on the
SLPI's own buses, not on an apps QUP, so iOS sensors go through booting the SLPI (PAS 12) the way
0300 boots the ADSP. logs/sensors/plan.md has the chain; this is its first step and boots nothing.
Boot-arg slpi=1 (with or without adsp=N; alone it runs only the ADSP's read-only stage 1, which maps
SMEM) adds one probe after stage 1, in sweet_adsp.c's thread:
- pil_slpi_mem (enchilada2.dtb slpi_region 0x96800000 + 0x1400000) against the kernel's RAM, and
  the conflict with display scanout slot 3 (0264/0319, sweetzc_slots=3 puts it in that region);
- the apps<->slpi SMEM partition (hosts 0/3, found by stage 1's ptable walk, mapped read-only) and
  items 424 (global, crash reason), 430/481 (SMP2P out/in), 478/479/480 (GLINK);
- slpi.mdt + the 19 slpi.bNN files from modem_a (UFS LUN 4) at the offsets of tools/mss-fw-table.py's
  logic, crc32-checked (slpi_fw[], from modem_a.img whose sha256 matches the phone's sde4); the ELF
  header + hash segment must be the whole mdt and the relocatable image (0x1180000 bytes) must fit
  the region.
It ends in one "SWEET SLPI: probe: ok/FAILED: ..." line; with sweetzc_slots=3 it reports FAILED
(region taken by scanout slot 3) after all checks. Nothing is stored, no SCM call is made and the
region itself is never mapped. The ADSP stages are unchanged; "done" no longer says "stopped early"
for adsp=0. Not yet built in CI or booted.

